      "problem": "Factor ${s}^{4}-{s}^{2}-12.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $t={s}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{4}-{s}^{2}-12 & ={({s}^{2})}^{2}-({s}^{2})-12 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-t-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $s:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t-12 & =(t+3)(t-4) \\\\  & =({s}^{2}+3)({s}^{2}-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
